# Copied verbatim into dist/ by `expo export -p web` and applied by Cloudflare's
# asset server.
#
# This file lives in public/ because that is the only directory Expo copies
# through to the build output. It was previously only present in dist/, which
# meant the next build silently dropped it.
#
# Matching rules are *appended*, not overridden — two rules that both set
# Cache-Control produce one concatenated header and the first max-age wins. So
# Cache-Control is set only on the hashed paths below, never on /*, and the HTML
# shells keep the asset server's own no-cache default.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# Content-hashed by Metro — a new build means a new URL, so these never go stale.
/_expo/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
